* ''A shared act never makes a shared secret'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; four ratcheted research rounds, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026`>>). Every act that touches more than one face sorts one of three ways: its private bytes DISSOLVE into the owning face's records (D), its public bytes stand at the FLOOR by design (F), or it names a vessel SECRET (S) whose principal and opener the house names record by record. A mixed carrier splits before it sorts. The browser holds no vessel key: founding, fleet join, slot changes, roster, archives, handle book, dyads, restore and clear sort D or F, so each tab asks only its own face's unlock and public floor work asks nothing. Phones, installed web apps, probes, the CLI, MCP and watcher seats and a native shell hold no S. A tablet waking floor carries ciphertext and public records unattended and decrypts no face's record. A container restarts at its floor and nothing unlocks it unattended. A guest island that owns a key store stands as its own vessel. A node holds S only for records it names: the serving key has no record yet, so it guards nothing today. * ''The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; a fifth research round, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026`>> #/the-place-signer). A node's place identity keeps a KEL whose inception commits the next key, and that next key rides the founding card beside the seed charter's cold next key, offline; the online place signer runs unattended for an enumerated allowlist of floor duties alone (the KEL's own events excepted, which the card's key signs), rests under the host's TPM-bound credential where the host offers one and an owner-only file elsewhere, and never rides an environment, an image or a log. A stolen online signer rotates away by the card; a lost card beside a stolen signer re-founds. The floor holds no custody key; it holds its own named place signer. The format change rides the founding bake (`X0`). The place KEL commits its next cold key on the founding card and rotates by that card (`W29`), and the seed census names every reach of the seed past the floor, K15's owed bonds among them (`tools/seed-census.mjs`).

